body:
TermAl install procedure (integration owner): never rebuild in place in the live master checkout's target/. On DL560/Linux, `cargo clean --release -p termal` plus an in-place build left /home/greg/github/TermAl/target/release/termal ABSENT for about 4 min (seen at 00:14:42Z on 2026-11-08, during the ba6c9846 install), so sessions' TERMAL_CLI path was missing. Correct procedure:
- build in a separate CARGO_TARGET_DIR (e.g. target/install-target);
- copy the new binary beside the live one as target/release/termal.new;
- back up the old one with a hard link or copy (termal.<sha8>.bak);
- `mv -f termal.new termal`, an atomic rename, so the path never disappears.
On Windows: rename the running termal.exe aside, then immediately copy or rename the new one in from the same volume.
